# Tangerine Compiler — Change Budget (audit §36)
# Self-hosting compiler written in Tangerine
#
# budget_verify checks the §36 envelope SemanticDelta ⊆ ChangeBudget: a
# ChangeBudget is the audit's per-change allowance over ONE §31 SemanticDelta
# — the stable symbol keys the change may create/remove/modify/affect, the
# SEMANTIC ALLOWANCE SETS naming the exact public-api / abi / effect /
# capability / unsafe-site changes it may make (third audit item 28 — sets
# are PRIMARY over the counts), the public-api / abi row counts (the
# documented fallback), the effect classes / capability edges a NEW row may
# carry (the fallback), the new unsafe markers it may add, the contract
# evolution it may perform (the kind-aware compatibility orientation of
# third audit item 27), the refactor-equivalence requirement (third audit
# item 32 — a configured minimum §41 EquivalenceLevel plus whether a proof
# is demanded; evaluated by budget_verify_with_equivalence) and (optionally)
# the alloc-class effect rows it may introduce plus the RESERVED allocation
# byte budget. The module reads ONLY
# SemanticDelta / EquivalenceResult records (semantic_delta.tg +
# equivalence.tg, never AST / typed / MIR state)
# and mirrors the semantic_delta.tg / repair_candidates.tg idioms. An EMPTY
# budget (ChangeBudget {} / budget_refactor_default()) admits only the empty
# delta: budget_verified returns false for any non-empty change — the
# fail-closed default that mechanically prevents scope creep.
#
# DOMAIN ADAPTATIONS (the audit names mapped onto the §31 records that exist
# — the §29 module doc's adaptation discipline, never invented look-alikes):
#   - StableSymbolId is the §27 stable symbol identity (stable_ids.tg
#     section 6): its DECLARATION lineage (StableDeclId) is the budget's
#     membership identity (audit item 5). allowed_symbols is a
#     Set[StableDeclId]; membership compares the 128-bit digest words
#     (stable_decl_eq), so the canonical key TEXT a violation line renders
#     is the attached cargo — a signature-only edit keeps the declaration
#     and is therefore allowed exactly when the declaration is.
#   - EffectId is the §11 dirty-class id. The §31 effect deltas carry typed
#     EffectSummaryView values (audit item 14 — bits = the dirty word of
#     semantic_summary_dirty_word: allocate=1, block=2, io=4, spawn=8,
#     sleep=16, panic=32, unsafe=64; capabilities = the capability-id texts
#     of the summary's capability set). allow_new_effects therefore names
#     CLASS ids: an EffectId { id: <class bit> } entry allows that class;
#     ids outside the class band {1,2,4,8,16,32,64} can never match an
#     effect delta (a budget entry outside the band is inert — fail-closed,
#     never permissive).
#   - CapabilityId is types.tg's fixed capability id, as keyed in the §31
#     capability row text "cap<id>" (arena=1, mmio=2, ...).
#   - Unsafe markers (audit item 16): SemanticDelta.unsafe_delta now carries
#     the unsafe-surface facts — created/removed UnsafeFact rows (semantic_
#     model.tg; the snapshot's unsafe_facts table, diffed by the delta
#     core). max_new_unsafe counts ONLY the created UnsafeFact rows — the
#     ownership-row counting rule is gone (the §31 ownership rows are not an
#     unsafe surface).
#   - Contract relations (audit items 17 + 27): a clause's identity rides the
#     row's StableContractId key (function + kind word + canonical clause
#     text), so a clause TEXT change never produces a Modified contract row
#     — it produces a Removed row (old text) + a Created row (new text).
#     Check 4 compares the before/after ContractSemantic projections
#     through semantic_delta.tg's contract_relation_of — the structured
#     strengthening/weakening comparison over the CANONICAL clause trees
#     (the item's prover subset, documented in its section of
#     semantic_delta.tg): equal trees Equivalent; (x ∧ y) ⇒ x conjunct
#     containment; the numeric-bound lattice of the comparison words over
#     identical operand texts with int-literal bounds. contract_relation_of
#     is orientation-NEUTRAL; check 4 maps relation + kind through
#     semantic_delta.tg's contract_compatibility_of (third audit item 27):
#     Pre + Strengthened and Post + Weakened are Breaking (old callers /
#     consumers become illegal), Pre + Weakened and Post + Strengthened are
#     Compatible, any non-Equivalent Invariant change is Breaking, and any
#     Incomparable is Unknown (not provably safe). THE CONTRACT POLICY IS
#     LAYERED: allow_contract_weakening (true) skips the contract checks
#     entirely — the coarse pre-item-27 escape hatch; otherwise
#     allow_contract_evolution (false by default, the zero-delta contract
#     policy budget_refactor_default() names) rejects EVERY non-Equivalent
#     change whatever its classification; when evolution is authorized
#     (true), Compatible passes while Breaking and Unknown violate. Every
#     Removed row replaced by a Created row of the same (function, kind
#     word) is paired positionally (both lists keep the delta's sorted
#     clause-text order; the k-th removed clause pairs with the k-th
#     created clause) and the pair's relation decides. A Removed row
#     WITHOUT a same-(function, kind) Created row (after None) is Weakened
#     (contract_relation_of(Some, None)); pure clause additions (Created
#     rows without a Removed pairing — before None) are Strengthened
#     (contract_relation_of(None, Some)) and the kind decides: a Pre /
#     Invariant addition is Breaking, a Post addition Compatible (the
#     zero-delta policy rejects every non-Equivalent change either way); a
#     Modified row (same clause id on both sides — only the declared
#     MESSAGE can differ, the constraint content rides the key) is
#     Equivalent; a function deleted from the program is already gated by
#     allowed_symbols (its rows are excluded here). The §31 contract rows
#     carry no visibility flag, so the orientation gate applies to EVERY
#     surviving function's clauses — the conservative direction (the audit
#     frames the rule for public functions; private contract churn is
#     gated too, never skipped).
#   - Semantic allowance sets (third audit item 28): five Set[String] fields
#     name the exact changes a budget authorizes. They are PRIMARY: when a
#     domain's set is non-empty, budget_verify tests each row's canonical
#     key and the count / class gate is NOT consulted; when the set is
#     empty, the pre-item-28 count (or class allow-set) is the documented
#     fallback. Row keys: public-api rows key on the stable symbol key (the
#     text after the second space of the snapshot writer's
#     "<digest> <kind> <key>" row); abi rows key on the "symbol=<key>"
#     component of semantic_abi_surface_row_text (a pre-item-18 fallback
#     row IS the pub-Function key, so it keys as itself); effect additions
#     key on the effect row's function key; capability additions key on the
#     typed "fn|cap<id>" row key (both the capability delta rows and the
#     effect-summary capability additions normalize to it); unsafe additions
#     key on the fact's site text ("" for a site-less marker).
#
# THE CHECKS (each violation string starts with "budget:"):
#   1. allowed_symbols — every key of delta.created / delta.removed /
#      delta.affected and every modified entity's stable_id must be allowed.
#      A key reported through several lists (affected contains the created/
#      removed seeds) yields one violation per list — deterministic.
#   2. public-api rows — the symmetric-difference rows of the
#      public_api_delta before/after views (semantic_delta_rows_diff).
#      Audit item 28 precedence: when allowed_public_api_changes is
#      non-empty, each row's stable key must be in the set (one row
#      violation otherwise); when the set is empty, the pre-item-28 count
#      rule fires — a row count above max_public_api_delta lists every
#      differing row.
#   3. abi rows — abi_delta's symmetric-difference rows likewise, against
#      allowed_abi_changes (primary) and max_abi_delta (empty-set
#      fallback).
#   4. contract evolution — the kind-aware compatibility gate (audit items
#      17 + 27; see the adaptation above): skipped when
#      allow_contract_weakening is true; otherwise the zero-delta default
#      policy (allow_contract_evolution = false) rejects every
#      non-Equivalent relation, and the evolution-authorized policy
#      rejects the Breaking / Unknown classifications. PAIRED replacements,
#      unpaired REMOVED clauses (Weakened) and unpaired ADDED clauses
#      (Strengthened) all flow through the same gate.
#   5. added effect classes (audit item 15) — for EVERY effect delta row,
#      each class bit the row's AFTER view sets that its BEFORE view does
#      not (added_bits = after.bits & !before.bits, evaluated per class
#      bit) is a new effect. Audit item 28 precedence: when
#      allowed_effect_additions is non-empty, the row is allowed iff its
#      function key is in the set (one violation per added class
#      otherwise); when the set is empty, the pre-item-28 class allow-set
#      (allow_new_effects) is the fallback. Row lifecycle never
#      participates: a row whose summary gained a class on an
#      already-rowed function fires exactly like a Created row (Created =
#      the before view is empty) — the Modified-effect bypass is closed.
#   6. added capabilities (audit items 15 + 28) — each capability delta row
#      whose capability edge is Present after and was Absent before
#      (created edges; a CapabilityDelta row exists only when the presence
#      changed) and whose "fn|cap<id>" key is not in
#      allowed_capability_additions is a violation when that set is
#      non-empty; when the set is empty, the "cap<id>" id must be in
#      allow_new_capabilities (the fallback). Also, per effect delta row,
#      each capability-id text the AFTER view carries that the BEFORE view
#      does not (added_caps = after.capabilities − before.capabilities)
#      keys the same way (the effect view's raw id text normalizes to
#      "fn|cap<id>") — one violation per (row, capability).
#   7. new unsafe markers (audit items 16 + 28) — Audit item 28 precedence:
#      when allowed_unsafe_sites is non-empty, each CREATED UnsafeFact
#      row's site must be in the set; when the set is empty, the
#      pre-item-28 count rule fires — a count above max_new_unsafe lists
#      every counted marker row. EXACT COUNTING RULE: the count is the
#      number of CREATED UnsafeFact rows (delta.unsafe_delta.created) — the
#      created rows of the unsafe-facts table only.
#   8. allocation — only when max_allocation_delta = Some(n): the count of
#      effect delta rows whose after view newly carries the alloc class
#      (bit 1 — the §11 payload marks allocation as the word's low bit); a
#      count above n lists every counted row. The RESERVED allocation byte
#      budget allocation_budget_bytes = Some(n) additionally fails closed:
#      the §11 effect view the delta carries (bits + capability ids)
#      contains NO allocation byte count — no snapshot row or delta payload
#      serializes allocation bytes — so the verifier cannot derive a
#      bytes-used value from a SemanticDelta and reports the precise gap
#      instead of silently passing a declared byte cap. (A future
#      byte-carrying effect payload plugs in here; the field and this gate
#      are the wiring point.)
#   9. refactor equivalence — ONLY in budget_verify_with_equivalence (the
#      envelope verifier budget_verify holds no §41 result): when the
#      budget declares equivalence_requirement = Some(req), the supplied
#      Option[EquivalenceResult] must satisfy it — a result that is proven
#      (equivalence_result_is_proven) and whose EquivalenceLevel ranks at
#      or above req.minimum_level on equivalence.tg's ladder, or (only when
#      req.require_proven = false) a TestedNoCounterexample run. A missing
#      result and an insufficient result each yield ONE
#      "budget:equivalence-required" row (Unknown and Counterexample never
#      satisfy; tests are evidence, never proof — audit item 55).
#
# VIOLATION CATALOG (the exact strings budget_verify emits; every row listed
# is prefixed "budget:" on its own line, in the check order above):
#   budget:symbol-created <key> not in allowed_symbols
#   budget:symbol-removed <key> not in allowed_symbols
#   budget:symbol-modified <key> not in allowed_symbols
#   budget:symbol-affected <key> not in allowed_symbols
#   budget:public-api row <row> not in allowed_public_api_changes (key <key>)
#   budget:public-api <n> rows exceed max_public_api_delta <m>
#   budget:public-api row <row>
#   budget:abi row <row> not in allowed_abi_changes (key <key>)
#   budget:abi <n> rows exceed max_abi_delta <m>
#   budget:abi row <row>
#   budget:contract-breaking <fn-key> <kind> <old-clause> -> <new-clause>
#     (<relation>; compatibility <word>; policy <zero-delta|orientation>;
#     allow_contract_evolution=<b>) — a replaced clause whose compatibility
#     classification (or the zero-delta policy) violates the contract
#     policy (the relation word is Equivalent|Strengthened|Weakened|
#     Incomparable; the compatibility word is Compatible|Breaking|Unknown)
#   budget:contract-breaking <fn-key> <kind> <clause> (clause removed on a
#     surviving function; compatibility <word>; policy
#     <zero-delta|orientation>; allow_contract_evolution=<b>)
#   budget:contract-breaking <fn-key> <kind> <clause> (clause added on a
#     surviving function; compatibility <word>; policy
#     <zero-delta|orientation>; allow_contract_evolution=<b>)
#   budget:effect <fn-key> introduces class <class-word> (EffectId <bit>) not
#     in allowed_effect_additions
#   budget:effect <fn-key> introduces class <class-word> (EffectId <bit>) not
#     in allow_new_effects
#   budget:capability <fn-key> cap<id> not in allowed_capability_additions
#     (key <fn-key>|cap<id>)
#   budget:capability <fn-key> capability <cap-id-text> not in
#     allowed_capability_additions (key <fn-key>|cap<id>)
#   budget:capability <fn-key> cap<id> not in allow_new_capabilities
#   budget:capability <fn-key> capability <cap-id-text> not in
#     allow_new_capabilities
#   budget:unsafe marker <marker-row> site not in allowed_unsafe_sites
#   budget:unsafe <n> new-unsafe markers exceed max_new_unsafe <m>
#   budget:unsafe marker <function> <kind-word>[:<site>]
#   budget:allocation <n> added alloc-class effect rows exceed
#     max_allocation_delta <m>
#   budget:allocation row <fn-key>
#   budget:allocation-bytes <n> cannot be verified: the semantic delta
#     carries no allocation byte payload (effect views are bits + capability
#     ids only); allocation_budget_bytes is reserved
#   budget:equivalence-required missing equivalence result: minimum
#     <level-word> (require_proven=<b>) — check 9, only in
#     budget_verify_with_equivalence
#   budget:equivalence-required <result-render> does not satisfy the budget
#     minimum <level-word> (require_proven=<b>) — the supplied result's
#     level word + detail render names what fell short
#
# budget_verified is the Bool gate over the same envelope; an empty budget
# verifies only an empty delta. budget_verify_with_equivalence /
# budget_verified_with_equivalence extend those with check 9.

use std::core::{Option}
use std::collections::{Vec, Set}

use tg_compiler::ids::{EffectId}
use tg_compiler::types::{CapabilityId}
use tg_compiler::stable_ids::{StableDeclId, stable_decl_of_key, stable_decl_eq}
use tg_compiler::semantic_delta::{
  SemanticDelta, EffectDelta, Presence, ContractDelta, ContractSemantic, ContractRelation,
  ContractCompatibility, contract_relation_of, contract_relation_word,
  contract_compatibility_of, contract_compatibility_word,
  AbiDeltaView, AbiSurfaceView, EffectSummaryView, CapabilityDelta,
  semantic_delta_rows_diff, semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text, semantic_delta_empty
}
# (third audit item 32) The refactor-equivalence gate reads the §41 result
# vocabulary: the configured minimum is an EquivalenceLevel, and the
# satisfaction decision is equivalence_result_satisfies (equivalence.tg's
# proven-level ladder — tests are evidence, never proof).
use tg_compiler::equivalence::{
  EquivalenceLevel, EquivalenceResult, equivalence_level_word,
  equivalence_result_render, equivalence_result_satisfies,
  equivalence_structural, equivalence_proven_finite, equivalence_tested,
  equivalence_unknown, equivalence_counterexample
}

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The §36 protocol record
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The refactor-equivalence requirement (third audit item 32): a budget may
# declare the minimum §41 equivalence LEVEL a change must carry as
# evidence, and whether that evidence must be a PROOF. minimum_level ranks
# along equivalence.tg's equivalence_level_rank ladder among the three
# PROVEN levels (StructurallyEquivalent < ProvenForFiniteDomain <
# ProvenUnderConstraints); require_proven = true (the default and the
# budget_refactor_default() policy) additionally rejects
# TestedNoCounterexample — a corpus run is evidence, not proof (audit item
# 55). The requirement is evaluated ONLY by
# budget_verify_with_equivalence: budget_verify holds no result and checks
# the envelope alone.
struct EquivalenceRequirement
  # The minimum proven level the change's EquivalenceResult must reach.
  minimum_level: EquivalenceLevel = EquivalenceLevel::StructurallyEquivalent
  # Whether the result must be a proof: true rejects the evidence-only
  # TestedNoCounterexample level.
  require_proven: Bool = true
end

# The per-change allowance over ONE SemanticDelta (the audit's struct, field
# for field). Every field is defaulted so an EMPTY budget is expressible as
# ChangeBudget {}: empty allow-sets, zero row budgets, no allocation cap,
# zero-delta contract policy (allow_contract_evolution = false) and the
# coarse contract override off — the fail-closed envelope.
struct ChangeBudget
  # The stable DECLARATION identities the change may touch (audit item 5):
  # every created/removed/modified/affected key must parse to a declaration
  # whose digest words equal an entry's. A signature-only edit keeps the
  # declaration (the item-6 split), so it is allowed exactly when the
  # declaration is.
  allowed_symbols: Set[StableDeclId] = Set::new()
  # The most public-api rows (symmetric-difference surface rows) the change
  # may introduce. The EMPTY-set fallback of allowed_public_api_changes
  # (third audit item 28).
  max_public_api_delta: Int = 0
  # The most abi rows the change may introduce. The EMPTY-set fallback of
  # allowed_abi_changes.
  max_abi_delta: Int = 0
  # The §11 dirty-class ids an effect delta may newly introduce (the
  # domain adaptation in the module doc: class id = dirty-word bit). The
  # EMPTY-set fallback of allowed_effect_additions.
  allow_new_effects: Set[EffectId] = Set::new()
  # The capability ids a capability edge / effect-summary capability may
  # newly introduce. The EMPTY-set fallback of allowed_capability_additions.
  allow_new_capabilities: Set[CapabilityId] = Set::new()
  # The most new unsafe markers the change may add (created UnsafeFact
  # rows — the exact counting rule in the doc). The EMPTY-set fallback of
  # allowed_unsafe_sites.
  max_new_unsafe: Int = 0
  # The coarse pre-item-27 contract override: true skips the contract
  # evolution checks entirely (every contract change is permitted).
  allow_contract_weakening: Bool = false
  # The kind-aware contract-evolution policy (third audit item 27): false
  # (the default and the budget_refactor_default() policy) allows ZERO
  # contract deltas — every non-Equivalent relation violates whatever its
  # compatibility classification; true applies
  # contract_compatibility_of(kind, relation): Compatible passes, Breaking
  # and Unknown violate.
  allow_contract_evolution: Bool = false
  # The public-api rows the change may introduce by stable symbol key
  # (semantic set, third audit item 28). PRIMARY when non-empty;
  # max_public_api_delta is the empty-set fallback.
  allowed_public_api_changes: Set[String] = Set::new()
  # The abi rows the change may introduce by "symbol=<key>" (semantic set).
  allowed_abi_changes: Set[String] = Set::new()
  # The effect rows that may newly carry effect classes, keyed by the
  # effect row's function key (semantic set). PRIMARY when non-empty;
  # allow_new_effects is the empty-set fallback.
  allowed_effect_additions: Set[String] = Set::new()
  # The capability additions allowed, keyed by the typed "fn|cap<id>" row
  # key (semantic set — capability delta rows and effect-summary
  # capability additions share the key). PRIMARY when non-empty;
  # allow_new_capabilities is the empty-set fallback.
  allowed_capability_additions: Set[String] = Set::new()
  # The unsafe marker SITES allowed on newly created UnsafeFact rows
  # (semantic set — the fact's site text; "" keys a site-less marker).
  # PRIMARY when non-empty; max_new_unsafe is the empty-set fallback.
  allowed_unsafe_sites: Set[String] = Set::new()
  # The most effect rows newly carrying the alloc class permitted; None =
  # no cap.
  max_allocation_delta: Option[Int] = Option::None
  # The RESERVED allocation byte budget (third audit item 28): None = no
  # byte cap. The §11 effect view a delta carries serializes bits +
  # capability ids and NO allocation byte count, so no bytes-used value is
  # derivable from a SemanticDelta today; Some(n) fails closed on the
  # reservation (check 8) instead of silently passing.
  allocation_budget_bytes: Option[Int] = Option::None
  # (third audit item 32) The refactor-equivalence requirement: None (the
  # default) imposes no equivalence gate; Some(req) makes
  # budget_verify_with_equivalence require an EquivalenceResult that
  # satisfies req — a missing or insufficient result is the
  # "budget:equivalence-required" violation (check 9).
  equivalence_requirement: Option[EquivalenceRequirement] = Option::None
end

# The default-refactor budget (third audit items 27 + 32): the documented
# constructor for the strictest contract policy — ALLOW ZERO contract
# deltas — AND the default refactor-equivalence requirement (minimum
# StructurallyEquivalent, require_proven true). The contract policy is the
# defaulted ChangeBudget {} policy (every count 0, every set empty,
# allow_contract_evolution = false, allow_contract_weakening = false): a
# non-Equivalent contract change — even a compatibility-Compatible one
# (Pre + Weakened / Post + Strengthened) — is a violation unless the caller
# EXPLICITLY authorizes it, and the change must additionally carry at least
# a structurally-equivalent PROOF through budget_verify_with_equivalence.
# The name pins the policy: a mechanically refactored change must not
# evolve any public contract and must be proven equivalent at the
# configured level unless a human/budget author explicitly relaxes it.
pub def budget_refactor_default() -> ChangeBudget
  budget_refactor_with_level(EquivalenceLevel::StructurallyEquivalent, true)
end

# The refactor budget with a CONFIGURED equivalence requirement (third
# audit item 32 — "ChangeBudget::refactor() requires EquivalenceResult >=
# configured level"): minimum_level defaults to StructurallyEquivalent and
# require_proven to true; the contract policy is the same zero-delta
# policy budget_refactor_default() carries. Callers that accept a
# differential/property run as evidence (no proof demand) pass
# require_proven = false.
pub def budget_refactor_with_level(
  minimum_level: EquivalenceLevel = EquivalenceLevel::StructurallyEquivalent,
  require_proven: Bool = true
) -> ChangeBudget
  ChangeBudget {
    equivalence_requirement: Option::Some(EquivalenceRequirement {
      minimum_level: minimum_level,
      require_proven: require_proven
    })
  }
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Text / kind primitives (the semantic_delta.tg byte-text idioms)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# The integer value of the leading ASCII-digit run of a text (0 when the
# text does not start with a digit). The capability text "cap<id>" is
# sliced past its "cap" prefix before this runs. Byte-parse idiom mirrors
# semantic_slice.tg's slice_text_to_int.
def budget_int_prefix(s: String) -> Int
  var value = 0
  var i = 0
  while i < s.len() do
    let bs = s.slice(i, i + 1).bytes()
    if bs.len() == 0 then
      break
    end
    let b = bs[0] as Int
    if b >= 48 && b <= 57 then
      value = value * 10 + (b - 48)
      i = i + 1
    else
      break
    end
  end
  value
end

# The capability id of a §31 capability-part text ("cap<id>"); -1 for any
# other text (a -1 id can never match a budget entry — ids are fixed
# positive CapabilityId numbers, arena=1 / mmio=2).
def budget_cap_id_of(part: String) -> Int
  if !part.starts_with("cap") then
    return -1
  end
  if part.len() <= 3 then
    return -1
  end
  var digits = part.slice(3, part.len())
  budget_int_prefix(digits)
end

# The capability-id TEXT of an effect view's capability entry (an
# effect-delta capability is the raw id text, not a "cap<id>" word — the
# budget membership check parses it the same way).
def budget_effect_cap_id_of(id_text: String) -> Int
  budget_int_prefix(id_text)
end

# Whether a §11 dirty word carries the class of the given bit (the word is
# the sum of its class bits: allocate=1, block=2, io=4, spawn=8, sleep=16,
# panic=32, unsafe=64 — semantic_summary_dirty_word's field order).
def budget_word_has_class(word: Int, bit: Int) -> Bool
  (word / bit) % 2 == 1
end

# The class word of a §11 dirty-class bit (the §11 may_* field names minus
# the "may_" prefix; the fallback keeps the word deterministic for any bit).
def budget_class_text(bit: Int) -> String
  if bit == 1 then "alloc"
  elsif bit == 2 then "block"
  elsif bit == 4 then "io"
  elsif bit == 8 then "spawn"
  elsif bit == 16 then "sleep"
  elsif bit == 32 then "panic"
  else "unsafe"
  end
end

# Whether the AFTER view of an effect row newly carries the class bit
# (after.bits & !before.bits, evaluated per bit — audit item 15: the
# lifecycle of the row never participates).
def budget_effect_added_class(row: EffectDelta, bit: Int) -> Bool
  budget_word_has_class(row.after.bits, bit) &&
    !budget_word_has_class(row.before.bits, bit)
end

# Whether the AFTER view of an effect row newly carries the capability id
# (added_caps = after.capabilities − before.capabilities).
def budget_effect_added_cap(row: EffectDelta, id_text: String) -> Bool
  if row.before.capabilities.contains(&id_text) then
    return false
  end
  row.after.capabilities.contains(&id_text)
end

# The subject function key of a contract row: the StableContractId key's
# first component (the fn digest key — everything before the first '|';
# contract ids always open with the fn key).
def budget_contract_fn_key(contract_id: String) -> String
  var i = 0
  while i < contract_id.len() do
    if contract_id.slice(i, i + 1) == "|" then
      return contract_id.slice(0, i)
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  contract_id.clone()
end

# The kind word of a contract row: the before side's kind when the clause
# existed before, else the after side's kind ("" when the row carries no
# side — a both-None row is never emitted).
def budget_contract_row_kind(row: ContractDelta) -> String
  match row.before
  when Option::Some(bv) then bv.kind.clone()
  when Option::None then
    match row.after
    when Option::Some(av) then av.kind.clone()
    when Option::None then "".to_string()
    end
  end
end

# Whether a contract relation violates the CONTRACT POLICY (third audit
# item 27) — the kind-aware compatibility gate:
#   - allow_contract_weakening = true: the coarse pre-item-27 override —
#     no contract relation is checked (every contract change is permitted).
#   - allow_contract_evolution = false (the default and the
#     budget_refactor_default() policy): ZERO contract deltas — every
#     non-Equivalent relation violates, whatever its classification.
#   - allow_contract_evolution = true: contract_compatibility_of(kind,
#     relation) decides — Compatible passes, Breaking and Unknown violate
#     (Unknown = Incomparable / unknown kind word: not provably safe).
def budget_contract_relation_violates(
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  kind: String,
  rel: ContractRelation
) -> Bool
  if budget.allow_contract_weakening then
    return false
  end
  if !budget.allow_contract_evolution then
    return !budget_contract_relation_equivalent(&rel)
  end
  match contract_compatibility_of(&kind, &rel)
  when ContractCompatibility::Compatible then false
  when ContractCompatibility::Breaking then true
  when ContractCompatibility::Unknown then true
  end
end

# Whether a relation is Equivalent (the zero-delta contract policy line).
def budget_contract_relation_equivalent(rel: ContractRelation) -> Bool
  match rel
  when ContractRelation::Equivalent then true
  when _ then false
  end
end

def budget_bool_text(b: Bool) -> String
  if b then "true" else "false" end
end

# The compatibility word of a relation under a kind word (the violation
# rows render this).
def budget_contract_compat_word(kind: String, rel: ContractRelation) -> String
  contract_compatibility_word(&contract_compatibility_of(&kind, &rel))
end

# The contract policy word of a budget ("orientation" = the kind-aware
# compatibility gate decides; "zero-delta" = the default-refactor policy
# rejects every non-Equivalent change).
def budget_contract_policy_word(budget: ChangeBudget) -> String
  if budget.allow_contract_evolution then "orientation" else "zero-delta" end
end

# The violation text of a replaced contract clause (a Removed row paired
# positionally with a Created row of the same function + kind word).
def budget_contract_pair_violation_text(
  fn_key: String,
  kind_word: String,
  old_text: String,
  new_text: String,
  rel: ContractRelation,
  budget: ChangeBudget
) -> String
  "budget:contract-breaking " + fn_key + " " + kind_word + " " + old_text +
    " -> " + new_text + " (" + contract_relation_word(&rel) + "; compatibility " +
    budget_contract_compat_word(&kind_word, &rel) + "; policy " +
    budget_contract_policy_word(&budget) + "; allow_contract_evolution=" +
    budget_bool_text(budget.allow_contract_evolution) + ")"
end

# The violation text of a clause removed on a surviving function
# (contract_relation_of(Some, None) is Weakened for every kind; the KIND
# decides the classification, never the render).
def budget_contract_removed_violation_text(
  fn_key: String,
  kind_word: String,
  clause_text: String,
  rel: ContractRelation,
  budget: ChangeBudget
) -> String
  "budget:contract-breaking " + fn_key + " " + kind_word + " " + clause_text +
    " (clause removed on a surviving function; compatibility " +
    budget_contract_compat_word(&kind_word, &rel) + "; policy " +
    budget_contract_policy_word(&budget) + "; allow_contract_evolution=" +
    budget_bool_text(budget.allow_contract_evolution) + ")"
end

# The violation text of a clause ADDED to a surviving function
# (contract_relation_of(None, Some) is Strengthened for every kind; the
# KIND decides — a Pre / Invariant addition is compatibility-Breaking, a
# Post addition is Compatible; the zero-delta policy rejects every
# addition).
def budget_contract_added_violation_text(
  fn_key: String,
  kind_word: String,
  clause_text: String,
  rel: ContractRelation,
  budget: ChangeBudget
) -> String
  "budget:contract-breaking " + fn_key + " " + kind_word + " " + clause_text +
    " (clause added on a surviving function; compatibility " +
    budget_contract_compat_word(&kind_word, &rel) + "; policy " +
    budget_contract_policy_word(&budget) + "; allow_contract_evolution=" +
    budget_bool_text(budget.allow_contract_evolution) + ")"
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Budget set membership (audit item 5: the allow-set holds TYPED stable
# declaration identities — Set[StableDeclId], Eq/Hash over the digest
# words — and membership compares those words; the delta key TEXTS the
# violation lines render are parsed at this boundary, once per printed
# check).
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# Whether a stable declaration identity is in allowed_symbols (digest-word
# equality — the item-6 declaration identity, never a text compare).
def budget_decl_allowed(budget: ChangeBudget, key: StableDeclId) -> Bool
  for s in budget.allowed_symbols do
    if stable_decl_eq(&s, &key) then
      return true
    end
  end
  false
end

# Whether a delta key text is allowed: the canonical key's DECLARATION
# identity must be in allowed_symbols (a signature-only edit keeps the
# declaration and is allowed exactly when the declaration is).
def budget_symbol_allowed(budget: ChangeBudget, key: String) -> Bool
  budget_decl_allowed(&budget, stable_decl_of_key(&key))
end

# Whether a §11 dirty-class id is in allow_new_effects (id equality — the
# identity is the id, never a name).
def budget_effect_allowed(budget: ChangeBudget, eid: EffectId) -> Bool
  for e in budget.allow_new_effects do
    if e.id == eid.id then
      return true
    end
  end
  false
end

# Whether a capability id is in allow_new_capabilities.
def budget_capability_allowed(budget: ChangeBudget, cap_id: Int) -> Bool
  for c in budget.allow_new_capabilities do
    if c.id == cap_id then
      return true
    end
  end
  false
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Semantic allowance rows (third audit item 28): the five allowed_* sets
# key on the delta rows' canonical keys — the sets are PRIMARY and the
# pre-item-28 count / class gates are the empty-set fallback.
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

# The public-api row key of a surface row text ("<digest> <kind> <stable
# key>" — the delta_public_api_rows grammar): the stable symbol key after
# the SECOND space. A malformed row (fewer than two spaces) keys as itself
# (fail-closed: membership then requires the exact text).
def budget_public_api_row_key(row: String) -> String
  var spaces = 0
  var i = 0
  while i < row.len() do
    if row.slice(i, i + 1) == " " then
      spaces = spaces + 1
      if spaces == 2 then
        return row.slice(i + 1, row.len())
      end
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  row.clone()
end

# The abi row key of a surface row text: the "symbol=<key>" component of
# semantic_abi_surface_row_text ("surface=...;symbol=<key>;..."). A
# pre-item-18 fallback row IS the pub-Function stable key (no "symbol="
# component), so it keys as itself.
def budget_abi_row_key(row: String) -> String
  for part in row.split(";") do
    if part.starts_with("symbol=") then
      return part.slice(7, part.len())
    end
  end
  row.clone()
end

# The canonical key of a capability addition: the typed row-key grammar
# "fn.key|cap<id>" shared by the capability delta rows and the
# effect-summary capability additions.
def budget_capability_addition_key(fn_key: String, cap_id: Int) -> String
  fn_key + "|cap" + cap_id.to_string()
end

# The allocation-class row count of a delta: the effect rows whose after
# view newly carries the alloc class (bit 1). Shared by the
# max_allocation_delta count check and the reserved byte-budget gate's gap
# row.
def budget_allocation_alloc_row_count(delta: SemanticDelta) -> Int
  var count = 0
  for row in delta.effect_delta do
    if budget_effect_added_class(&row, 1) then
      count = count + 1
    end
  end
  count
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# THE VERIFIER — SemanticDelta ⊆ ChangeBudget
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# Runs the §36 checks in the module doc's numbered order; deterministic —
# the delta's own sorted row order is preserved inside every check. The
# effect/capability checks read the typed before/after values of the §31
# rows (audit items 14 + 15): only what a row NEWLY introduces (added bits,
# added capabilities, presence toggles) fires — row lifecycle never
# participates.

pub def budget_verify(budget: ChangeBudget, delta: SemanticDelta) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()

  # The §11 dirty-class band (module doc: class ids = word bits).
  var class_bits: Vec[Int] = Vec::from([1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64])

  # 1. allowed_symbols — created / removed / modified / affected keys.
  for key in delta.created do
    if !budget_symbol_allowed(&budget, key.clone()) then
      out.push("budget:symbol-created " + key.clone() + " not in allowed_symbols")
    end
  end
  for key in delta.removed do
    if !budget_symbol_allowed(&budget, key.clone()) then
      out.push("budget:symbol-removed " + key.clone() + " not in allowed_symbols")
    end
  end
  for entry in delta.modified do
    if !budget_symbol_allowed(&budget, entry.stable_id.clone()) then
      out.push("budget:symbol-modified " + entry.stable_id.clone() + " not in allowed_symbols")
    end
  end
  for key in delta.affected do
    if !budget_symbol_allowed(&budget, key.clone()) then
      out.push("budget:symbol-affected " + key.clone() + " not in allowed_symbols")
    end
  end

  # 2. public-api rows — the symmetric-difference rows of the before/after
  #    surface views (empty when the surfaces are equal). Third audit item
  #    28 precedence: allowed_public_api_changes is PRIMARY when non-empty
  #    (each row's stable symbol key must be named); the count cap is the
  #    empty-set fallback.
  let api_rows = semantic_delta_rows_diff(&delta.public_api_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.public_api_delta.after.rows)
  if budget.allowed_public_api_changes.len() > 0 then
    for row in api_rows do
      let key = budget_public_api_row_key(&row)
      if !budget.allowed_public_api_changes.contains(&key) then
        out.push("budget:public-api row " + row + " not in allowed_public_api_changes (key " +
          key + ")")
      end
    end
  elsif api_rows.len() > budget.max_public_api_delta then
    out.push("budget:public-api " + api_rows.len().to_string() +
      " rows exceed max_public_api_delta " + budget.max_public_api_delta.to_string())
    for row in api_rows do
      out.push("budget:public-api row " + row)
    end
  end

  # 3. abi rows — the audit item-28 precedence of allowed_abi_changes and
  #    the max_abi_delta fallback.
  let abi_rows = semantic_delta_rows_diff(&delta.abi_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.abi_delta.after.rows)
  if budget.allowed_abi_changes.len() > 0 then
    for row in abi_rows do
      let key = budget_abi_row_key(&row)
      if !budget.allowed_abi_changes.contains(&key) then
        out.push("budget:abi row " + row + " not in allowed_abi_changes (key " + key + ")")
      end
    end
  elsif abi_rows.len() > budget.max_abi_delta then
    out.push("budget:abi " + abi_rows.len().to_string() +
      " rows exceed max_abi_delta " + budget.max_abi_delta.to_string())
    for row in abi_rows do
      out.push("budget:abi row " + row)
    end
  end

  # 4. contract evolution (audit items 17 + 27) — the contract_relation_of
  #    relation + the contract kind map through contract_compatibility_of;
  #    the budget policy (allow_contract_weakening and
  #    allow_contract_evolution) decides whether the classification
  #    violates. Every
  #    Removed row replaced by a Created row of the same (function, kind
  #    word) is paired positionally (both lists keep the delta's sorted
  #    clause-text order) and the pair's relation decides. A Removed row
  #    with no same-(function, kind) Created row (after None) is Weakened
  #    (the clause was dropped on a surviving function); pure additions are
  #    Strengthened; a Modified row (same clause key on both sides — only
  #    the message can differ) is Equivalent; deleted functions (keys in
  #    delta.removed) are the symbol gate's.
  if !budget.allow_contract_weakening then
    var r = 0
    while r < delta.contract_delta.len() do
      let row_r = delta.contract_delta[r]
      let fn_key = budget_contract_fn_key(&row_r.contract_id)
      if delta.removed.contains(&fn_key) then
        # A deleted function — its contract rows are the symbol gate's.
        r = r + 1
      else
        # The surviving function's contiguous row run (the delta's rows are
        # key-sorted and fn keys never contain '|').
        var run_end = r + 1
        var in_run = true
        while run_end < delta.contract_delta.len() && in_run do
          let row_e = delta.contract_delta[run_end]
          if budget_contract_fn_key(&row_e.contract_id) == fn_key then
            run_end = run_end + 1
          else
            in_run = false
          end
        end
        # The kind sub-runs of the run: the rows of one (function, kind
        # word) sort contiguously and keep their clause-text order.
        var k = r
        while k < run_end do
          let row_k = delta.contract_delta[k]
          let kind_word = budget_contract_row_kind(&row_k)
          var k_end = k + 1
          var in_kind = true
          while k_end < run_end && in_kind do
            let row_e2 = delta.contract_delta[k_end]
            if budget_contract_row_kind(&row_e2) == kind_word then
              k_end = k_end + 1
            else
              in_kind = false
            end
          end
          # Collect the sub-run's removed (before Some, after None) and
          # created (before None, after Some) clause projections in row
          # order; evaluate Modified rows on sight.
          var removed_rows: Vec[ContractSemantic] = Vec::new()
          var created_rows: Vec[ContractSemantic] = Vec::new()
          var m = k
          while m < k_end do
            let row = delta.contract_delta[m]
            match row.before
            when Option::Some(bv) then
              match row.after
              when Option::Some(av) then
                # A Modified row: the same clause key on both sides — the
                # canonical text rides the key, so only the message can
                # differ and contract_relation_of is Equivalent; the check
                # is defensive.
                let b_text = bv.canonical_text.clone()
                let a_text = av.canonical_text.clone()
                let rel_before = Option::Some(bv)
                let rel_after = Option::Some(av)
                let rel = contract_relation_of(&rel_before, &rel_after)
                if budget_contract_relation_violates(&budget, &kind_word, &rel) then
                  out.push(budget_contract_pair_violation_text(&fn_key, &kind_word,
                    &b_text, &a_text, &rel, &budget))
                end
              when Option::None then
                removed_rows.push(bv)
              end
            when Option::None then
              match row.after
              when Option::Some(av) then
                created_rows.push(av)
              when Option::None then ()
              end
            end
            m = m + 1
          end
          # The positional pairing: the k-th removed clause vs the k-th
          # created clause of the (function, kind word) — the item's
          # replaced-clause comparison.
          var pair_i = 0
          while pair_i < removed_rows.len() && pair_i < created_rows.len() do
            let pair_before = Option::Some(removed_rows[pair_i].clone())
            let pair_after = Option::Some(created_rows[pair_i].clone())
            let rel = contract_relation_of(&pair_before, &pair_after)
            if budget_contract_relation_violates(&budget, &kind_word, &rel) then
              out.push(budget_contract_pair_violation_text(&fn_key, &kind_word,
                &removed_rows[pair_i].canonical_text, &created_rows[pair_i].canonical_text,
                &rel, &budget))
            end
            pair_i = pair_i + 1
          end
          # Unpaired Removed rows (after None): the clause was dropped on a
          # surviving function — contract_relation_of(Some, None) is
          # Weakened; the KIND decides whether that is compatibility-safe
          # (Pre) or breaking (Post / Invariant).
          while pair_i < removed_rows.len() do
            let gone_before = Option::Some(removed_rows[pair_i].clone())
            let gone_after: Option[ContractSemantic] = Option::None
            let rel = contract_relation_of(&gone_before, &gone_after)
            if budget_contract_relation_violates(&budget, &kind_word, &rel) then
              out.push(budget_contract_removed_violation_text(&fn_key, &kind_word,
                &removed_rows[pair_i].canonical_text, &rel, &budget))
            end
            pair_i = pair_i + 1
          end
          # Unpaired Created rows (before None) are pure clause additions —
          # contract_relation_of(None, Some) is Strengthened; the KIND
          # decides (a Pre / Invariant addition is compatibility-Breaking,
          # a Post addition is Compatible; the zero-delta policy rejects
          # every addition). The item-27 correction applies here too: a
          # stronger precondition breaks old callers however it arrived.
          while pair_i < created_rows.len() do
            let add_before: Option[ContractSemantic] = Option::None
            let add_after = Option::Some(created_rows[pair_i].clone())
            let rel = contract_relation_of(&add_before, &add_after)
            if budget_contract_relation_violates(&budget, &kind_word, &rel) then
              out.push(budget_contract_added_violation_text(&fn_key, &kind_word,
                &created_rows[pair_i].canonical_text, &rel, &budget))
            end
            pair_i = pair_i + 1
          end
          k = k_end
        end
        r = run_end
      end
    end
  end

  # 5. added effect classes — every §11 class bit the after view newly
  #    carries (added_bits = after.bits & !before.bits — audit item 15;
  #    row lifecycle never participates: Created rows have an empty before
  #    view, Modified rows fire on their additions); one violation per
  #    (row, class). Third audit item 28 precedence: when
  #    allowed_effect_additions is non-empty the row is allowed iff its
  #    function key is named (allow_new_effects is NOT consulted); when the
  #    set is empty, the class allow-set is the fallback.
  for row in delta.effect_delta do
    for bit in class_bits do
      if budget_effect_added_class(&row, bit) then
        if budget.allowed_effect_additions.len() > 0 then
          if !budget.allowed_effect_additions.contains(&row.function) then
            out.push("budget:effect " + row.function.clone() + " introduces class " +
              budget_class_text(bit) + " (EffectId " + bit.to_string() +
              ") not in allowed_effect_additions")
          end
        else
          let eid = EffectId { id: bit }
          if !budget_effect_allowed(&budget, eid) then
            out.push("budget:effect " + row.function.clone() + " introduces class " +
              budget_class_text(bit) + " (EffectId " + bit.to_string() +
              ") not in allow_new_effects")
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end

  # 6. new capabilities — the created capability edges (presence toggles
  #    Absent -> Present) AND the capability ids an effect row's after view
  #    newly carries (added_caps = after.capabilities − before.capabilities).
  #    Third audit item 28 precedence: when
  #    allowed_capability_additions is non-empty, the addition's "fn|cap<id>"
  #    key must be named; when the set is empty, allow_new_capabilities is
  #    the fallback.
  for row in delta.capability_delta do
    match row.before
    when Presence::Present then ()
    when Presence::Absent then
      match row.after
      when Presence::Absent then ()
      when Presence::Present then
        let cap_id = budget_cap_id_of(row.capability)
        if cap_id >= 0 then
          if budget.allowed_capability_additions.len() > 0 then
            let key = budget_capability_addition_key(row.function.clone(), cap_id)
            if !budget.allowed_capability_additions.contains(&key) then
              out.push("budget:capability " + row.function.clone() + " cap" +
                cap_id.to_string() + " not in allowed_capability_additions (key " + key + ")")
            end
          elsif !budget_capability_allowed(&budget, cap_id) then
            out.push("budget:capability " + row.function.clone() + " cap" +
              cap_id.to_string() + " not in allow_new_capabilities")
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  for row in delta.effect_delta do
    for id_text in row.after.capabilities do
      if budget_effect_added_cap(&row, id_text) then
        let cap_id = budget_effect_cap_id_of(id_text)
        if cap_id >= 0 then
          let key = budget_capability_addition_key(row.function.clone(), cap_id)
          if budget.allowed_capability_additions.len() > 0 then
            if !budget.allowed_capability_additions.contains(&key) then
              out.push("budget:capability " + row.function.clone() + " capability " +
                id_text.clone() + " not in allowed_capability_additions (key " + key + ")")
            end
          elsif !budget_capability_allowed(&budget, cap_id) then
            out.push("budget:capability " + row.function.clone() + " capability " +
              id_text.clone() + " not in allow_new_capabilities")
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end

  # 7. new unsafe markers (audit items 16 + 28) — third audit item 28
  #    precedence: when allowed_unsafe_sites is non-empty, each CREATED
  #    UnsafeFact row's site must be named; when the set is empty, the
  #    pre-item-28 count rule fires (the CREATED UnsafeFact rows only).
  if budget.allowed_unsafe_sites.len() > 0 then
    for fact in delta.unsafe_delta.created do
      if !budget.allowed_unsafe_sites.contains(&fact.site) then
        out.push("budget:unsafe marker " + semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text(&fact) +
          " site not in allowed_unsafe_sites")
      end
    end
  else
    let unsafe_count = delta.unsafe_delta.created.len()
    if unsafe_count > budget.max_new_unsafe then
      out.push("budget:unsafe " + unsafe_count.to_string() +
        " new-unsafe markers exceed max_new_unsafe " + budget.max_new_unsafe.to_string())
      for fact in delta.unsafe_delta.created do
        out.push("budget:unsafe marker " + semantic_delta_unsafe_marker_text(&fact))
      end
    end
  end

  # 8. allocation — only under an explicit Some(n) count cap: the effect
  #    delta rows whose after view newly carries the alloc class (bit 1).
  #    The RESERVED allocation byte budget fails closed when set: the
  #    delta carries no allocation byte payload (the §11 view is bits +
  #    capability ids), so no bytes-used value is derivable (see the
  #    module doc's check 8).
  match budget.max_allocation_delta
  when Option::Some(max_alloc) then
    let alloc_count = budget_allocation_alloc_row_count(&delta)
    if alloc_count > max_alloc then
      out.push("budget:allocation " + alloc_count.to_string() +
        " added alloc-class effect rows exceed max_allocation_delta " +
        max_alloc.to_string())
      for row in delta.effect_delta do
        if budget_effect_added_class(&row, 1) then
          out.push("budget:allocation row " + row.function.clone())
        end
      end
    end
  when Option::None then
    ()
  end
  match budget.allocation_budget_bytes
  when Option::Some(max_bytes) then
    out.push("budget:allocation-bytes " + max_bytes.to_string() +
      " cannot be verified: the semantic delta carries no allocation byte payload " +
      "(effect views are bits + capability ids only); allocation_budget_bytes is reserved")
  when Option::None then
    ()
  end

  out
end

# The Bool gate over the same envelope: true exactly when the delta verifies
# (no violations — the empty budget admits only the empty delta).
pub def budget_verified(budget: ChangeBudget, delta: SemanticDelta) -> Bool
  budget_verify(&budget, &delta).len() == 0
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# (third audit item 32) The refactor-equivalence gate
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# budget_verify checks the §36 ENVELOPE only: it holds no §41
# EquivalenceResult and therefore cannot evaluate an
# EquivalenceRequirement. Callers that hold the change's equivalence
# evidence use budget_verify_with_equivalence: it extends budget_verify's
# rows with ONE "budget:equivalence-required" violation when the budget
# declares a requirement and the supplied result is missing or
# insufficient. The satisfaction decision is equivalence.tg's
# equivalence_result_satisfies: a PROVEN result whose level ranks at or
# above the configured minimum satisfies; TestedNoCounterexample
# satisfies ONLY when require_proven = false (tests are evidence, not
# proof — audit item 55); Unknown and Counterexample never satisfy.

# The missing-result row: the budget demanded evidence and none was
# supplied.
def budget_equivalence_missing_text(req: EquivalenceRequirement) -> String
  "budget:equivalence-required missing equivalence result: minimum " +
    equivalence_level_word(req.minimum_level) + " (require_proven=" +
    budget_bool_text(req.require_proven) + ")"
end

# The insufficient-result row: the supplied result's render (level word +
# detail) names exactly what fell short of the configured requirement.
def budget_equivalence_insufficient_text(
  req: EquivalenceRequirement,
  r: EquivalenceResult
) -> String
  "budget:equivalence-required " + equivalence_result_render(&r) +
    " does not satisfy the budget minimum " + equivalence_level_word(req.minimum_level) +
    " (require_proven=" + budget_bool_text(req.require_proven) + ")"
end

# The requirement decision: Option::None when the budget declares no
# requirement or the supplied result satisfies it; Option::Some(row) = the
# single violation row.
def budget_equivalence_violation(
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  equivalence: Option[EquivalenceResult]
) -> Option[String]
  match budget.equivalence_requirement
  when Option::None then Option::None
  when Option::Some(req) then
    match equivalence
    when Option::None then Option::Some(budget_equivalence_missing_text(&req))
    when Option::Some(r) then
      if equivalence_result_satisfies(&r, req.minimum_level, req.require_proven) then
        Option::None
      else
        Option::Some(budget_equivalence_insufficient_text(&req, &r))
      end
    end
  end
end

# budget_verify PLUS the item-32 equivalence gate: the envelope's
# violations (empty = the delta fits the budget) followed by the single
# "budget:equivalence-required" row when the budget declares a requirement
# that the supplied result does not satisfy. A budget with no requirement
# yields exactly budget_verify's rows.
pub def budget_verify_with_equivalence(
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  delta: SemanticDelta,
  equivalence: Option[EquivalenceResult]
) -> Vec[String]
  var out = budget_verify(&budget, &delta)
  match budget_equivalence_violation(&budget, equivalence)
  when Option::Some(row) then out.push(row)
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  out
end

# The Bool gate over budget_verify_with_equivalence: true exactly when the
# delta fits the envelope AND the equivalence requirement (if any) holds.
pub def budget_verified_with_equivalence(
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  delta: SemanticDelta,
  equivalence: Option[EquivalenceResult]
) -> Bool
  budget_verify_with_equivalence(&budget, &delta, equivalence).len() == 0
end

# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The third-audit item-27 / item-28 / item-32 budget lane (unit-style rows)
# ———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
# The sibling style of semantic_delta.tg's contract_relation_lane_check:
# the rows are self-checking helpers the test-file lane
# (tests/change_budget_test.tg) calls. Each row builds a minimal
# SemanticDelta fixture (the delta records ARE the verifier's input — no
# snapshot is needed) and asserts the budget verdict:
#   T1  Pre Strengthened under an evolution-authorized budget -> VIOLATION.
#       The audit item-27 correction: a stronger precondition breaks old
#       callers; the pre-item-27 rule accepted it.
#   T1b a pure Pre ADDITION is Strengthened -> VIOLATION (the correction
#       covers added clauses, not only replacements).
#   T2  Post Strengthened under the same budget -> accepted (compatibility
#       Compatible: the guarantee only grew).
#   T2b a pure Post ADDITION is Strengthened -> accepted (Compatible).
#   T3  Invariant Weakened under the same budget -> VIOLATION (any
#       non-Equivalent invariant change is Breaking).
#   T3b Pre Weakened under the same budget -> accepted (Compatible: the
#       caller obligation only shrank) — the contrast against T1.
#   T4  the semantic API set allows ONE specific public-api row while the
#       count cap is 0 (set PRIMARY); the empty-set control falls back to
#       the count cap and rejects — third audit item 28.
#   T5  budget_refactor_default() rejects ANY non-Equivalent contract
#       delta (even the Compatible Pre + Weakened pair) while the empty
#       delta verifies — the zero-delta default-refactor policy.
#   T6  the capability set allows the exact "fn|cap<id>" addition while
#       allow_new_capabilities is empty (set PRIMARY); the empty-set
#       control falls back to allow_new_capabilities and rejects.
#   T7  the effect set allows the function's added class while
#       allow_new_effects is empty (set PRIMARY); the empty-set control
#       falls back to allow_new_effects and rejects.
#   T8  a declared allocation_budget_bytes fails closed even on the empty
#       delta — the reserved field cannot be verified against a delta that
#       carries no allocation byte payload.
#   T9-T15 (third audit item 32) the refactor-equivalence gate over
#       budget_verify_with_equivalence:
#       T9  the default refactor budget with NO equivalence result ->
#           "budget:equivalence-required" (missing).
#       T10 a ProvenForFiniteDomain result satisfies the default minimum.
#       T11 a StructurallyEquivalent result satisfies the default minimum.
#       T12 TestedNoCounterexample VIOLATES while require_proven = true
#           (tests are evidence, not proof).
#       T13 the same tested result is accepted when the requirement carries
#           require_proven = false.
#       T14 Unknown and Counterexample never satisfy.
#       T15 a configured HIGHER minimum (ProvenForFiniteDomain) rejects a
#           weaker (structural) proof — the configured-level comparison.

def budget_lane_sem(kind: String, text: String) -> ContractSemantic
  ContractSemantic {
    kind: kind,
    expression_fingerprint: "".to_string(),
    canonical_text: text,
    message: Option::None
  }
end

# A replaced contract clause as the real diff emits it — a Removed row
# (before Some, after None) + a Created row (before None, after Some) under
# the same (function, kind word) — the item-17 pairing the budget check
# consumes.
def budget_lane_contract_pair(kind: String, before_text: String, after_text: String) -> SemanticDelta
  var delta = semantic_delta_empty()
  var rows: Vec[ContractDelta] = Vec::new()
  rows.push(ContractDelta {
    contract_id: "m::pub#fn()->unit|" + kind.clone() + "|" + before_text.clone(),
    before: Option::Some(budget_lane_sem(&kind, &before_text)),
    after: Option::None
  })
  rows.push(ContractDelta {
    contract_id: "m::pub#fn()->unit|" + kind.clone() + "|" + after_text.clone(),
    before: Option::None,
    after: Option::Some(budget_lane_sem(&kind, &after_text))
  })
  delta.contract_delta = rows
  delta
end

# A purely ADDED contract clause (Created row only) — the item-27 addition
# path: contract_relation_of(None, Some) is Strengthened, and the kind
# decides the compatibility.
def budget_lane_contract_added(kind: String, after_text: String) -> SemanticDelta
  var delta = semantic_delta_empty()
  var rows: Vec[ContractDelta] = Vec::new()
  rows.push(ContractDelta {
    contract_id: "m::pub#fn()->unit|" + kind.clone() + "|" + after_text.clone(),
    before: Option::None,
    after: Option::Some(budget_lane_sem(&kind, &after_text))
  })
  delta.contract_delta = rows
  delta
end

def budget_lane_api_delta(before_texts: Vec[String], after_texts: Vec[String]) -> SemanticDelta
  var delta = semantic_delta_empty()
  delta.public_api_delta = AbiDeltaView {
    surface_id: "api".to_string(),
    before: AbiSurfaceView { rows: before_texts },
    after: AbiSurfaceView { rows: after_texts }
  }
  delta
end

# One effect row whose after view newly carries classes (the added-class
# delta shape of check 5).
def budget_lane_effect_delta(function: String, before_bits: Int, after_bits: Int) -> SemanticDelta
  var delta = semantic_delta_empty()
  var rows: Vec[EffectDelta] = Vec::new()
  rows.push(EffectDelta {
    function: function,
    before: EffectSummaryView { bits: before_bits, capabilities: Vec::new() },
    after: EffectSummaryView { bits: after_bits, capabilities: Vec::new() }
  })
  delta.effect_delta = rows
  delta
end

# One created capability edge (Absent -> Present — the presence toggle of
# check 6).
def budget_lane_capability_delta(function: String, capability: String) -> SemanticDelta
  var delta = semantic_delta_empty()
  var rows: Vec[CapabilityDelta] = Vec::new()
  rows.push(CapabilityDelta {
    function: function,
    capability: capability,
    before: Presence::Absent,
    after: Presence::Present
  })
  delta.capability_delta = rows
  delta
end

# One assertion: the budget verdict matches the expectation (a mismatch row
# names the expected verdict and the actual violation list).
def budget_lane_expect(
  inout out: Vec[String],
  name: String,
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  delta: SemanticDelta,
  want_violation: Bool
) -> Unit
  let violations = budget_verify(&budget, &delta)
  if (violations.len() > 0) != want_violation then
    let verdict = if want_violation then "a violation" else "acceptance" end
    out.push(name + ": expected " + verdict + ", got [" + violations.join("; ") + "]")
  end
  ()
end

# Run the T1-T8 rows; the returned list names every mismatch (empty = the
# whole lane verifies). Exported for a behavior lane.
pub def budget_lane_check() -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()

  # The evolution-authorized budget: the kind orientation decides; the
  # count / set gates stay at their empty defaults.
  let evolution = ChangeBudget { allow_contract_evolution: true }

  # T1 — Pre Strengthened -> Breaking -> violation.
  let t1 = budget_lane_contract_pair("Pre",
    "bingt(ident(amount),int(0))", "bingt(ident(amount),int(1000))")
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T1-pre-strengthening-violates", &evolution, &t1, true)

  # T1b — a pure Pre ADDITION is Strengthened -> Breaking -> violation
  # (the item-27 correction covers additions, not just replacements).
  let t1b = budget_lane_contract_added("Pre", "bingt(ident(amount),int(1000))")
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T1b-pre-addition-violates", &evolution, &t1b, true)

  # T2 — Post Strengthened -> Compatible -> accepted.
  let t2 = budget_lane_contract_pair("Post",
    "bingt(ident(amount),int(0))", "bingt(ident(amount),int(1000))")
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T2-post-strengthening-compatible", &evolution, &t2, false)

  # T2b — a pure Post ADDITION is Strengthened -> Compatible -> accepted.
  let t2b = budget_lane_contract_added("Post", "bingt(ident(amount),int(1000))")
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T2b-post-addition-compatible", &evolution, &t2b, false)

  # T3 — Invariant Weakened -> Breaking -> violation.
  let t3 = budget_lane_contract_pair("Invariant",
    "bingt(ident(amount),int(0))", "binge(ident(amount),int(0))")
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T3-invariant-weakening-violates", &evolution, &t3, true)

  # T3b — Pre Weakened -> Compatible -> accepted.
  let t3b = budget_lane_contract_pair("Pre",
    "bingt(ident(amount),int(0))", "binge(ident(amount),int(0))")
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T3b-pre-weakening-compatible", &evolution, &t3b, false)

  # T4 — set membership over the count cap (third audit item 28): one
  # changed public-api row, count cap 0, the set naming the row's stable
  # key.
  let t4 = budget_lane_api_delta(
    Vec::from(["0xaa Function m::pub#fn()->unit"]),
    Vec::from(["0xbb Function m::pub#fn()->unit"]))
  var t4_set: Set[String] = Set::new()
  t4_set.insert("m::pub#fn()->unit".to_string())
  let t4_budget = ChangeBudget {
    max_public_api_delta: 0,
    allowed_public_api_changes: t4_set
  }
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T4-api-set-allows-specific-change", &t4_budget, &t4, false)
  # The empty-set control: the same delta under the count fallback (cap 0).
  let t4_control = ChangeBudget { max_public_api_delta: 0 }
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T4-api-count-fallback-rejects", &t4_control, &t4, true)

  # T5 — the default-refactor budget admits zero contract deltas: even the
  # Compatible Pre + Weakened pair violates; the empty delta verifies.
  let t5 = budget_lane_contract_pair("Pre",
    "bingt(ident(amount),int(0))", "binge(ident(amount),int(0))")
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T5-refactor-default-rejects-contract-delta",
    &budget_refactor_default(), &t5, true)
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T5-refactor-default-empty-delta-ok",
    &budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(), false)

  # T6 — the capability set (primary) allows the exact "fn|cap<id>"
  # addition while allow_new_capabilities is empty; the empty control
  # falls back and rejects.
  let t6 = budget_lane_capability_delta("m::pub#fn()->unit", "cap1")
  var t6_caps: Set[String] = Set::new()
  t6_caps.insert("m::pub#fn()->unit|cap1".to_string())
  let t6_budget = ChangeBudget { allowed_capability_additions: t6_caps }
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T6-capability-set-allows", &t6_budget, &t6, false)
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T6-capability-fallback-rejects",
    &ChangeBudget {}, &t6, true)

  # T7 — the effect set (primary) allows the function's added class while
  # allow_new_effects is empty; the empty control falls back and rejects.
  let t7 = budget_lane_effect_delta("m::pub#fn()->unit", 0, 4)
  var t7_effects: Set[String] = Set::new()
  t7_effects.insert("m::pub#fn()->unit".to_string())
  let t7_budget = ChangeBudget { allowed_effect_additions: t7_effects }
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T7-effect-set-allows", &t7_budget, &t7, false)
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T7-effect-fallback-rejects",
    &ChangeBudget {}, &t7, true)

  # T8 — the RESERVED allocation byte budget fails closed: a budget that
  # declares allocation_budget_bytes rejects even the empty delta (no
  # delta-side byte payload exists to verify the cap).
  let t8_budget = ChangeBudget { allocation_budget_bytes: Option::Some(4096) }
  budget_lane_expect(&mut out, "T8-allocation-bytes-reserved-fails-closed",
    &t8_budget, &semantic_delta_empty(), true)

  # T9-T15 (third audit item 32) — the refactor-equivalence gate.
  # T9: the default refactor budget requires equivalence — no result supplied
  # is the missing-result violation.
  budget_lane_equivalence_expect(&mut out, "T9-refactor-equivalence-missing-violates",
    &budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(), Option::None, true)
  # T10: a ProvenForFiniteDomain proof satisfies the default minimum.
  budget_lane_equivalence_expect(&mut out, "T10-finite-proof-passes",
    &budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(),
    Option::Some(equivalence_proven_finite("symbolic-finite")), false)
  # T11: a StructurallyEquivalent proof satisfies the default minimum.
  budget_lane_equivalence_expect(&mut out, "T11-structural-proof-passes",
    &budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(),
    Option::Some(equivalence_structural("normalized-mir")), false)
  # T12: TestedNoCounterexample is evidence, not proof — with
  # require_proven = true it violates.
  budget_lane_equivalence_expect(&mut out, "T12-tested-not-a-proof-violates",
    &budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(),
    Option::Some(equivalence_tested(true, "the differential corpus")), true)
  # T13: the same tested result passes when the requirement does not demand
  # a proof (require_proven = false).
  budget_lane_equivalence_expect(&mut out, "T13-tested-evidence-passes-without-proof-demand",
    &budget_refactor_with_level(EquivalenceLevel::StructurallyEquivalent, false),
    &semantic_delta_empty(),
    Option::Some(equivalence_tested(true, "the differential corpus")), false)
  # T14: Unknown and Counterexample never satisfy.
  budget_lane_equivalence_expect(&mut out, "T14-unknown-never-satisfies",
    &budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(),
    Option::Some(equivalence_unknown("no layer proved equivalence")), true)
  budget_lane_equivalence_expect(&mut out, "T14b-counterexample-never-satisfies",
    &budget_refactor_default(), &semantic_delta_empty(),
    Option::Some(equivalence_counterexample("()", "1", "2")), true)
  # T15: a configured HIGHER minimum rejects a weaker proof (the
  # configured-level comparison).
  budget_lane_equivalence_expect(&mut out, "T15-weaker-proof-below-minimum-violates",
    &budget_refactor_with_level(EquivalenceLevel::ProvenForFiniteDomain, true),
    &semantic_delta_empty(), Option::Some(equivalence_structural("normalized-mir")), true)

  out
end

# The equivalence-gate assertion: the verdict of
# budget_verify_with_equivalence must match the expectation (a mismatch row
# names the expected verdict and the actual violation list).
def budget_lane_equivalence_expect(
  inout out: Vec[String],
  name: String,
  budget: ChangeBudget,
  delta: SemanticDelta,
  equivalence: Option[EquivalenceResult],
  want_violation: Bool
) -> Unit
  let violations = budget_verify_with_equivalence(&budget, &delta, equivalence)
  if (violations.len() > 0) != want_violation then
    let verdict = if want_violation then "a violation" else "acceptance" end
    out.push(name + ": expected " + verdict + ", got [" + violations.join("; ") + "]")
  end
  ()
end
